{
    "map": {
        "description": "Masks pixels based on their color or by clipping a range of values. The output of this tool is used as an input to the Color Balance Mosaic Dataset tool to eliminate areas such as clouds and water that can skew the statistics used to color balance multiple images.",
        "generate_method.descr": "<xdoc><p>Create your mask based on the color of the pixels or by clipping high and low values.</p><ul><li><span title=\"COLOR_MASK\">Color mask</span>—Set the maximum color values to include in the output. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"HISTOGRAM_PERCENTAGE\">Histogram percentage</span>—Remove a percentage of high and low pixel values.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "generate_method.domain.COLOR_MASK": "Color mask",
        "generate_method.domain.HISTOGRAM_PERCENTAGE": "Histogram percentage",
        "generate_method.title": "Generate Method",
        "in_raster.descr": "The raster or mosaic dataset layer that you want to mask.",
        "in_raster.title": "Input Raster",
        "max_black.descr": "The maximum black value to exclude. The default is 0.",
        "max_black.title": "Maximum Black",
        "max_blue.descr": "The maximum blue value to exclude. The default is 255.",
        "max_blue.title": "Maximum Blue",
        "max_cyan.descr": "The maximum cyan value to exclude. The default is 255.",
        "max_cyan.title": "Maximum Cyan",
        "max_green.descr": "The maximum green value to exclude. The default is 255.",
        "max_green.title": "Maximum Green",
        "max_magenta.descr": "The maximum magenta value to exclude. The default is 255.",
        "max_magenta.title": "Maximum Magenta",
        "max_red.descr": "The maximum red value to exclude. The default is 255.",
        "max_red.title": "Maximum Red",
        "max_white.descr": "The maximum white value to exclude. The default is 255.",
        "max_white.title": "Maximum White",
        "max_yellow.descr": "The maximum yellow value to exclude. The default is 255.",
        "max_yellow.title": "Maximum Yellow",
        "out_raster.descr": "<xdoc><p>The name, location and format for the dataset you are creating. When storing a raster dataset in a geodatabase, do not add a file extension to the name of the raster dataset. When storing your raster dataset to a JPEG file, a JPEG 2000 file, or a geodatabase, you can specify a <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Compression</span> type and <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Compression Quality</span> within the Environment Settings.</p></xdoc>",
        "out_raster.title": "Output Raster Dataset",
        "params.category1": "Color Mask",
        "params.category2": "Histogram Percentage",
        "percentage_high.descr": "Exclude this percentage of the highest pixel values. The default is 100.",
        "percentage_high.title": "High Percentage",
        "percentage_low.descr": "Exclude this percentage of the lowest pixel values. The default is 0.",
        "percentage_low.title": "Low Percentage",
        "pixel_type.descr": "<xdoc><p>Choose the pixel depth of your input raster dataset. 8-bit is the default value; however, raster datasets with a greater bit-depth will need to have the color mask and histogram values scaled accordingly.</p><ul><li><span title=\"8_BIT\">8 bit</span>—The input raster dataset has values from 0 to 255. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"11_BIT\">11 bit</span>—The input raster dataset has values from 0 to 2047.</li><li><span title=\"12_BIT\">12 bit</span>—The input raster dataset has values from 0 to 4095.</li><li><span title=\"16_BIT\">16 bit</span>—The input raster dataset has values from 0 to 65535.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "pixel_type.domain.11_BIT": "11 bit",
        "pixel_type.domain.12_BIT": "12 bit",
        "pixel_type.domain.16_BIT": "16 bit",
        "pixel_type.domain.8_BIT": "8 bit",
        "pixel_type.title": "Pixel Type",
        "title": "Generate Exclude Area"
    }
}
